# environment.pdl - air and heat per room (owner 2026-10-25: oxygen / gas / temperature layers, fun first, realistic columns kept). Re-read every 2 s, no rebuild.
# Design: BOOK 16.game/RPG-SPACE-COLLISION-AND-DESTRUCTION-DESIGN.md 4b, 4c, 7e. State: state/air.txt (room|o2|temp|breach), one row per room; breach 1 = a hole in the hull, the room leaks.
# ENV | key | value | what it does
ENV | enabled        | 1    | 0 = nobody chokes, nothing leaks
ENV | tick_ms        | 2000 | ms between air updates
ENV | o2_ok          | 16   | oxygen percent below which a character chokes
ENV | choke_pm       | 30   | per-mille of max hp lost per tick while choking (at least 1 hp)
ENV | scrub_per_tick | 1    | percent of oxygen the ship's air recycler gives back per tick (up to the room's own level) when the room has no hole
ENV | leak_pct       | 12   | percent of the gap to the outside lost per tick through a hole (at least 1)
ENV | breach_speed   | 4    | a collision at this speed or more punctures breach_room
ENV | breach_room    | bridge | the room a collision punctures (later: the hull cell that was hit)
ENV | cold_c         | 5    | below this many degrees a character freezes
ENV | hot_c          | 45   | above this many degrees a character is scorched
ENV | temp_pm        | 20   | per-mille of max hp lost per tick while freezing or scorching (at least 1 hp)
ENV | cool_pct       | 6    | percent of the gap to the outside temperature a hole lets out per tick
ENV | warm_per_tick  | 2    | degrees per tick a sealed room heats or cools back to its own temperature
# OUTSIDE | o2 | temp   what lies beyond the hull
OUTSIDE | 0  | -150
# ROOM | id | o2 | temp   the level a room is kept at (rooms not listed: 21 percent, 20 C)
ROOM | bridge | 21 | 20
ROOM | engine | 21 | 38
ROOM | hold   | 21 | 12
